{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>הולך</b> [going]. Some say that this verse too concerns the sun, which inclines at times toward the north and toward the south, and they interpret <b>הרוח</b> [the wind] as 'side.' This is not correct. <b>ועל סביבותיו שב הרוח</b> [and on its circuits the wind returns] indicates this. The entire verse concerns the wind: at times the air moves toward the north side, at times toward the south side, and it circles from south to north along the east side, and from north to south along the west side. Therefore it says <b>סובב הולך הרוח</b> [going round, the wind goes], and in the end <b>ואל סביבותיו שב הרוח</b> [and to its circuits the wind returns] — like the return of the sun, for it is the cause of most of the wind's movements. Those who go down to the sea know of them, for they follow a single cycle in a day per year."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Resolved י״א as 'some say' (יש אומרים), standard abbreviation in Ibn Ezra."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:49.677738788Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}